  "findings": [
    "Inspected all76 native candidate frames on native cropped walk/melee and directional shooting boards. Copper-brown pressure body and green reagent inspection glass remain coherent. Simpler base equipment contrasts with Reinforced external green tanks.",
    "Six walking phases visibly alternate leg/support extension. Defend braces the body, hit recoils, turns show actual front/rear machinery and death folds/topples into the matching corpse. These are articulated painted actions; elapsed timing and feet sliding still require native game observation.",
    "Shoot14/15/16 aims one main pressure nozzle at up/level/down angles and paints charge/release/recovery. The repaired level shot has one open pressure outlet plus a rounded connected return fitting; the earlier extra-outlet/clipped-rim candidates are excluded. Green charge at frame4 is readable. Native actual projectile firing point and barrel recoil continuity remain unverified.",
    "Melee11/12/13 uses a working-arm swing rather than a copied ranged shot. Small green cap/nozzle emissions preserve brown metal texture. Native source body has no full450x400 canvas-edge cuts; board crops are diagnostic only.",
    "Base green equipment is deliberately less exposed than upgraded tanks; not every metal surface glows. Final comparative art/animation acceptance, native projectile timing, targeting and gameplay remain pending. Strict source-only validator checks exact full cohort, real master provenance, alpha and independent evidence; this review grants no asset/release acceptance."
